This repository does not vendor JUCE. The CMake build downloads JUCE 9.0.5.
JUCE is licensed separately, under the JUCE licence or the AGPLv3. Building
and distributing a binary that links JUCE means complying with that licence.
See https://juce.com/juce-9-licence/

ASIO support is optional and off by default. Enabling it uses Steinberg's
ASIO SDK headers (bundled with JUCE, or an SDK you supply) and the resulting
binary is also subject to the ASIO SDK licence terms.
